<title>LITHUANIA: LITHUANIA - YIELDS FALL ON 91-DAY T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIA - YIELDS FALL ON 91-DAY T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields on 91-day Lithuanian</p>
<p>Treasury bills fell at Tuesday's auction, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The average yield was 11.25 percent versus 11.37 percent at</p>
<p>the last auction for 91-day paper on March 17.</p>
<p>Not all of the 50 million litas issue was sold despite the</p>
<p>fact that it was oversubscribed.</p>
<p>The settlement date is March 28 and the maturity date is</p>
<p>June 27. </p>
<p>All figures in millions of litas.</p>
<p>SOLD    DAYS   MIN/MAX YIELD   AV. YIELD  LAST AV.YIELD  BID</p>
<p>38.643  91     10.70/11.95	 11.25	11.37	61.193</p>
<p>--Ed Stoddard, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
